    {
      "id": "afdd7a47-a09b-4e20-9824-405803c40dcd",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -880,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 640,
        "height": 720,
        "content": "## Verify phone numbers with a one-time SMS code (OTP)\n\n### How it works\nTwo webhooks give your sign-up or checkout form a phone verification step, with no code to host:\n1. **Request a code** (`POST /sms-otp/send` with `{ \"phone\": \"...\" }`) checks the number and sends a 6-digit code by SMS with the `generate_otp` tool of the SMS Vert Pro MCP server. The code is valid for 5 minutes.\n2. **Check a code** (`POST /sms-otp/verify` with `{ \"phone\": \"...\", \"code\": \"123456\" }`) checks it with `verify_otp`. A code works only once.\n3. Each verified number is added to a Google Sheet with the date, and the form gets a clear JSON answer: 200, 400 (invalid number), 401 (wrong or expired code), 429 (a code was already sent a moment ago).\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Create a Google Sheet with the columns `phone` and `verified_at`, and connect your Google account in **Log verified number**.\n2. Create a **Bearer Auth** credential with your SMS Vert Pro API V2 token (log in at smsvertpro.com, then open https://www.smsvertpro.com/api/doc-v2.php) and select it in the two MCP Client nodes.\n3. In **OTP settings**, set your sender name (11 characters max), your sheet URL, your default country code (numbers starting with 0 are converted) and the country codes you accept.\n4. Activate the workflow and call the two production webhook URLs from your form.\n\n### Customization\nReplace the Google Sheet with your CRM or database, or add a step that unlocks the user account once the number is verified."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
